Z||000019||DaRkLoRD||11-19-2000||05:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>My wing is at the paint shop being resanded down and re-painted. A mosquito died in the clear, so that had to be fixed.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Aww, you should have left it there so millions of years in the future, some other species can extract the blood to clone humans, in a futuristic theme park style zoo...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000020||1FST2M6||11-19-2000||07:50 PM||||this is the e-mail i sent spiral-max... i'll let you know what they say...<P>I was supplied one of your Spiral Max units by a friend. He swore he "felt a hp increase" I having Dyno tested every mod I've ever done on a Dynojet Model 248c. At Engineered Performance Inc. <A HREF="http://www.engineered.net" TARGET=_blank>www.engineered.net</A>  a shop owned by ASE Master Technicians and fellow Georgia Tech. graduates. We know how difficult it is to extract 20hp from anything. let alone an easy drop in unit like your spiral max. We ran a base line set of runs. I then followed the supplied directions. disconnecting the battery leads in order to erase any air/fuel or timing the e-prom may have in a "memory"  after a few Minutes of it being disconnected we reattached the leads and installed the unit per your instructions. and started the car, running it at varying speeds on the dyno for just over 3 full minutes. (all this testing was supervised by 2 ASE Certified Master Techs and myself ) we then shut the car off for a few minutes with fans facing the engine to not have any heat soak issues. with a Snap-on Reality 2 hooked to the car we started it back up to make sure the parameters were different from the following runs being sure the "memory" truly had been replaced with a new set of parameters. after seeing the settings WERE different and not in a safe mode" or "limp home mode" we ran a few tests 4 actually. as weak as the car is we didn't expect the results we got. my car made 103.6hp and 132.2lbft. with the spiral max unit installed it made LESS. on the 4th and final run nearly 30 minutes later we decided ok maybe we had it all wrong and decided to take out the unit and install it backwards. I didn't lose as must but still lost hp and Tq. with numbers posting at 102.3hp and 130.5lbft. how do you recommend I do testing so I MIGHT gain HP or TQ with your unit. any information you could relay would be much appreciated. I'll be sure to keep you posted with my results. Thanks in advance.<BR> <BR>Travis Hall<BR> <BR> <BR>ps. attached is the BEST of the dyno runs. and installed pictures.<BR>||||reg||1
