Z||000035||1FST2M6||11-21-2000||08:19 AM||||if you look in front of the car there is a 65mph wind fan.. we moved that directly in front of the intake for one run and saw no increase. I'm sure if we ducted the fan into the intake we'd see an increase but then we be running positive pressure not just the spiral max... which is what we were testing. These devices DO work on Carberated cars! I've seen dyno proof of that.. on "HotRod TV"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> but on ANYTHING with a throttle body, mass air(flapper door style) i have a hard time seeing how it can work at all.. there are too many obstructions to keep the air in their spiral/swirling effect. STILL nothing from spirl max... <P><BR>I sent those movies to ya Dark... hope you have winzip.  they range from 480meg to 1.4meg. ||||reg||1
